  "modified": "2026-08-25T17:33:09Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read after a Visual block put: do_put()\n     set the '] mark as bd.textcol + totlen - 1 without a lower bound, so a\n     blockwise register whose lines are all empty (y_width becomes -1 in\n     str_to_reg(), giving totlen 0) left the column at -1. With 'selection'\n     set to exclusive, nv_put() then passed that mark to inc(), which\n     dereferenced a pointer before the start of the line buffer.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-3520.patch: clamp curbuf->b_op_end.col to 0 in\n       src/ops.c; matches upstream patch 9.0.0765.\n     - CVE-2022-3520",
